This version keeps the 65536-entry lookup and its semantics, but shrinks each entry to one byte when the message count allows it.

- **When it applies:** if `MESGS < 255`, the table drops from 128 KB to 64 KB. This also halves the per-entry footprint for the common low message numbers, which should mean fewer cache misses.
- **Fallback:** otherwise it keeps 16-bit entries, as before.
- **Sentinel:** "not found" is the type's maximum value. That value can never be a valid index under the chosen width.
- **Duplicates:** the reverse fill is unchanged, so duplicate numbers still resolve to the first match.
- **Assumption:** this relies on `MESGS` being a compile-time constant (the conditional type needs it). I have not timed this change.

```cpp
const Profile::MESG* Profile::GetMesg(const FIT_UINT16 num)
{
    typedef typename std::conditional<((int)MESGS < 255), FIT_UINT8, FIT_UINT16>::type IdxT;
    struct Index
    {
        IdxT idx[65536];
        Index()
        {
            const IdxT none = (IdxT)~(IdxT)0;
            for (int k = 0; k < 65536; k++)
                idx[k] = none;
            for (int i = MESGS - 1; i >= 0; i--)
                idx[(FIT_UINT16)mesgs[i].num] = (IdxT)i;
        }
    };
    static const Index table;

    const IdxT i = table.idx[num];
    if (i == (IdxT)~(IdxT)0)
        return NULL;
    return &mesgs[i];
}
```

